1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,731
For months, Lena played the same four bars beautifully.

2
00:00:03,731 --> 00:00:07,462
They began a song nobody had heard, because she

3
00:00:07,462 --> 00:00:11,194
always stopped before the uncertain part.

4
00:00:11,614 --> 00:00:15,944
The rest existed in pencil. Crossed-out chords, fragments of

5
00:00:15,944 --> 00:00:20,275
words, a line she liked but did not understand

6
00:00:20,275 --> 00:00:24,605
yet. At home, unfinished could still mean possibility.

7
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:29,139
A cafe near the station hosted music on Thursdays.

8
00:00:29,139 --> 00:00:33,253
Two songs each. Beginners welcome. She saved the post,

9
00:00:33,253 --> 00:00:37,367
then searched the comments for reasons not to go.

10
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:40,500
One evening, she passed the cafe on her way

11
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,214
home. Through the window, someone was adjusting a microphone.

12
00:00:43,214 --> 00:00:45,928
She slowed down, pretended to read the menu, and

13
00:00:45,928 --> 00:00:48,642
kept walking.

14
00:00:49,062 --> 00:00:52,901
At home, she imagined the silence after a wrong

15
00:00:52,901 --> 00:00:56,740
note. Someone glancing at a phone. A polite smile.

16
00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:00,579
In her head, strangers were already disappointed.

17
00:01:00,999 --> 00:01:04,873
She practiced more. Practice helped, but every improvement moved

18
00:01:04,873 --> 00:01:08,747
the requirement further away. A cleaner opening. Another month

19
00:01:08,747 --> 00:01:12,621
before anyone could listen.

20
00:01:13,041 --> 00:01:15,807
Thursday became the day she was almost ready. She

21
00:01:15,807 --> 00:01:18,573
watched the evening pass from the kitchen, then felt

22
00:01:18,573 --> 00:01:21,339
relieved when it was too late to leave the

23
00:01:21,339 --> 00:01:24,105
apartment.

24
00:01:24,525 --> 00:01:27,796
Her notebook filled with performance dates she had not

25
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:31,067
attended. She had begun treating preparation as proof that

26
00:01:31,067 --> 00:01:34,338
she was moving, even when it kept her behind

27
00:01:34,338 --> 00:01:37,609
the same door.

28
00:01:38,029 --> 00:01:42,070
On the train, she heard a favorite musician talking

29
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:46,110
between songs. A chair scraped. Someone laughed. The room

30
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:50,150
sounded less perfect than she had imagined.

31
00:01:50,570 --> 00:01:53,871
She recorded the whole song. At each mistake, she

32
00:01:53,871 --> 00:01:57,172
wanted to restart. Instead, she stayed until the last

33
00:01:57,172 --> 00:02:00,473
chord faded.

34
00:02:00,893 --> 00:02:03,985
The recording was rough. She sent it to one

35
00:02:03,985 --> 00:02:07,076
friend with a specific question: does the second verse

36
00:02:07,076 --> 00:02:10,167
make sense? She did not ask whether she deserved

37
00:02:10,167 --> 00:02:13,258
to call herself a musician.

38
00:02:13,678 --> 00:02:16,630
Her friend pointed to a confusing line and an

39
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:19,582
image she remembered. Useful feedback, not a verdict on

40
00:02:19,582 --> 00:02:22,534
Lena or a promise that everybody would like her

41
00:02:22,534 --> 00:02:25,485
song.

42
00:02:25,905 --> 00:02:29,885
Lena drew the arrangement she had been living inside:

43
00:02:29,885 --> 00:02:33,864
imagine judgment, avoid the room, learn nothing new. This

44
00:02:33,864 --> 00:02:37,843
described her own pattern. It did not explain every

45
00:02:37,843 --> 00:02:41,823
person's fear of performing.

46
00:02:42,243 --> 00:02:45,052
She changed the line, finished a simple ending, and

47
00:02:45,052 --> 00:02:47,862
chose a date. Her goal was not to impress

48
00:02:47,862 --> 00:02:50,672
the room. It was to play one complete song

49
00:02:50,672 --> 00:02:53,481
in it.

50
00:02:53,901 --> 00:02:56,780
She messaged the organizer. Was there a place for

51
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:59,660
a first-time performer? The reply listed a time, a

52
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:02,539
short set, and where to put her name when

53
00:03:02,539 --> 00:03:05,418
she arrived.

54
00:03:05,838 --> 00:03:09,836
The details helped. They also made it real. On

55
00:03:09,836 --> 00:03:13,834
Thursday, Lena considered saying she was ill. She was

56
00:03:13,834 --> 00:03:17,831
frightened instead, and the distinction mattered to her.

57
00:03:18,251 --> 00:03:21,842
She packed her notebook, a water bottle, and the

58
00:03:21,842 --> 00:03:25,432
cable the organizer had mentioned. Then she checked the

59
00:03:25,432 --> 00:03:29,022
route. There were practical things she could prepare without

60
00:03:29,022 --> 00:03:32,613
rehearsing every possible reaction.

61
00:03:33,033 --> 00:03:36,173
Before leaving, she played the opening once. Her hand

62
00:03:36,173 --> 00:03:39,314
shook slightly. She decided not to keep testing whether

63
00:03:39,314 --> 00:03:42,454
the fear had disappeared. She had already checked that

64
00:03:42,454 --> 00:03:45,595
the instrument worked.

65
00:03:46,015 --> 00:03:49,695
Outside, the city carried on. Buses stopped. A delivery

66
00:03:49,695 --> 00:03:53,376
rider checked an address. Nobody was waiting to judge

67
00:03:53,376 --> 00:03:57,056
her walk to the cafe.

68
00:03:57,476 --> 00:04:00,733
At the entrance, she stopped. The sound of cups

69
00:04:00,733 --> 00:04:03,989
and conversation reached through the glass. She could still

70
00:04:03,989 --> 00:04:07,246
leave. Instead, she pushed the handle and stepped inside

71
00:04:07,246 --> 00:04:10,502
before deciding how to feel.

72
00:04:10,922 --> 00:04:13,520
The organizer showed her the sign-up sheet. Lena wrote

73
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:16,118
her name small, as though a smaller name might

74
00:04:16,118 --> 00:04:18,716
ask less of the room. Then she found somewhere

75
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:21,313
to sit.

76
00:04:21,733 --> 00:04:25,692
She drank water and watched another newcomer adjust the

77
00:04:25,692 --> 00:04:29,651
stool twice. Their first chord buzzed. They adjusted a

78
00:04:29,651 --> 00:04:33,610
finger and continued. The room continued with them.

79
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:37,165
Her new plan had three parts: prepare what she

80
00:04:37,165 --> 00:04:40,300
could, enter with the fear, listen afterward. It was

81
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:43,434
a plan for one evening, not a guarantee of

82
00:04:43,434 --> 00:04:46,569
confidence or applause.

83
00:04:46,989 --> 00:04:50,542
When her name was called, the distance to the

84
00:04:50,542 --> 00:04:54,094
microphone felt longer than it looked. She carried the

85
00:04:54,094 --> 00:04:57,647
notebook with both hands. The organizer lowered the stand.

86
00:04:58,067 --> 00:05:00,882
The first four bars came easily. Then she reached

87
00:05:00,882 --> 00:05:03,698
the part she had always interrupted. Her hand hesitated.

88
00:05:03,698 --> 00:05:06,513
A chord landed wrong, louder than the notes around

89
00:05:06,513 --> 00:05:09,329
it.

90
00:05:09,749 --> 00:05:13,089
For a second, she could hear only that mistake.

91
00:05:13,089 --> 00:05:16,430
She almost apologized. Instead, she took a breath, found

92
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:19,771
the next chord, and let the unfinished-sounding moment belong

93
00:05:19,771 --> 00:05:23,112
to the song.

94
00:05:23,532 --> 00:05:26,074
A line slipped from memory. She looked at the

95
00:05:26,074 --> 00:05:28,617
notebook. It was there to be used. Reading it

96
00:05:28,617 --> 00:05:31,160
did not cancel the hours she had spent making

97
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,702
the words her own.

98
00:05:34,122 --> 00:05:37,152
She reached the ending she had written that week.

99
00:05:37,152 --> 00:05:40,183
It was simple. The last note faded sooner than

100
00:05:40,183 --> 00:05:43,213
she expected, leaving a brief silence she no longer

101
00:05:43,213 --> 00:05:46,243
had to fill.

102
00:05:46,663 --> 00:05:50,885
People clapped. Some had listened closely; somebody had been

103
00:05:50,885 --> 00:05:55,107
distracted. It was a real room, containing several experiences

104
00:05:55,107 --> 00:05:59,329
at once. None was hers to control.

105
00:05:59,749 --> 00:06:02,536
Afterward, she could still feel her pulse in her

106
00:06:02,536 --> 00:06:05,322
wrists. Courage had not made her calm on command.

107
00:06:05,322 --> 00:06:08,109
She sat down, drank water, and listened to the

108
00:06:08,109 --> 00:06:10,895
next performer.

109
00:06:11,315 --> 00:06:14,438
Her friend asked how it went. Lena typed everything

110
00:06:14,438 --> 00:06:17,561
she had done wrong. Then added what the list

111
00:06:17,561 --> 00:06:20,684
had missed: I finished the song.

112
00:06:21,104 --> 00:06:24,846
Next morning, she noted two changes: slow the transition,

113
00:06:24,846 --> 00:06:28,587
mark the difficult lyric. She did not add become

114
00:06:28,587 --> 00:06:32,328
someone who never feels afraid. That was not something

115
00:06:32,328 --> 00:06:36,070
to practice.

116
00:06:36,490 --> 00:06:39,856
A week later, the cafe door looked familiar. She

117
00:06:39,856 --> 00:06:43,223
still paused before opening it. This time, the pause

118
00:06:43,223 --> 00:06:46,590
contained more than imagined judgment. It contained a memory

119
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:49,957
of getting through the song.

120
00:06:50,377 --> 00:06:53,367
There was no fearless version of Lena waiting behind

121
00:06:53,367 --> 00:06:56,356
the door. There was a person who could prepare,

122
00:06:56,356 --> 00:06:59,346
enter, listen, and return. She put her hand on

123
00:06:59,346 --> 00:07:02,335
the handle again.
